__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.FCBak
*.egg-info/
scratch/out/
.venv/
# A trailing comment is NOT a comment in .gitignore — the whole line is the
# pattern, spaces and '#' included, so `.venv-bempp/   # note` matched nothing and
# both of these venvs were tracked-able for their whole life. A `git add -A` duly
# swept 5,249 files and 2.1M lines of .venv-bempp into a commit. Comments go on
# their own line.
# dedicated bempp-cl venv (meshio>=5 clash isolation)
.venv-bempp/
# dedicated openEMS venv (GPL, source-built)
.venv-openems/
tests/reliability_cache/
tests/multiagent_cache/
# generated CAD artifacts (scratch/gen_artifacts.py output)
results/

# `python -m build` output (release flow: build -> twine check -> clean-venv install)
build/
dist/

# Legal / trademark filing correspondence. These carry the applicant's name,
# address and contact details, so they must not ride along into a repo that is
# headed for public. Keep the files on disk, keep them out of the history — the
# secret scan in CI does not look for PII, and history is forever once pushed.
*Filing-Record*
docs/*.docx
